# U-Boot defconfig — ONYX BOOX C67ML Magellan (RK3026, dual Cortex-A9)
#
# Modeled on the in-tree evb-rk3036 A9 board (same RK292x SPL memory layout:
# SPL runs from internal SRAM at 0x10080000, not DRAM) with C67ML specifics:
# UART2 console, SD/eMMC (dwmmc) boot, ACT8931 PMIC on I2C0.
#
# Storage note: the device's internal flash is RAW NAND behind a closed FTL
# (no mainline driver), so real boot media is the microSD card via dwmmc.
#
# RK3026 is Cortex-A9: no ARM architected generic timer, so U-Boot proper uses
# the DM Rockchip timer and the SPL uses a local __udelay() (rk3026-board-spl.c).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is now `make savedefconfig` canonical: every line below is one the
# build actually needs. It was hand-maintained until 2026-07-29 and had drifted
# to 199 lines, of which 138 were redundant or INERT. Six negations did nothing
# at all -- SPL_DM, SPL_BLK, DM_MMC, CMD_FAT, CMD_EXT4, CMD_FS_GENERIC -- while
# the file's comments asserted the opposite, which is how "the SPL is DM-free"
# survived as a premise for months. Round-trip verified: regenerating .config
# from this file gives a byte-identical .config.
#
# Keep it canonical. If you add a line, re-run savedefconfig and re-add comments
# rather than appending by hand.
#
# Defaults that are already off, so they need no line here, with the reasons
# worth keeping (each was established the hard way):
#
#   CMD_USB / CMD_GPT — not needed to load a zImage. (CMD_I2C is now ON, see the
#     i2c block below.)
#
#   ⚠️ "U-Boot stays FAT-only; EXT4 does not come back with CMD_FAT" — THIS WAS
#     FALSE, corrected 2026-07-31. The built .config has FS_EXT4=y, CMD_EXT4=y,
#     CMD_EXT2=y and CMD_FS_GENERIC=y, because BOOTSTD_DEFAULTS pulls in
#     BOOT_DEFAULTS_CMDS, which HARD-`select`s them (boot/Kconfig:425). A
#     defconfig negation cannot override a select; only dropping BOOTSTD_DEFAULTS
#     (itself merely `imply`'d, so negatable) removes them -- and that must
#     re-add CMD_BOOTZ and CMD_FAT explicitly in the same commit, or extlinux
#     silently boots nothing (CMD_BOOTZ has no `default y`; it exists only via
#     that same select, and pxe_utils.c falls through every arm without it).
#     (MMC and CMD_FAT/CMD_MMC were re-enabled 2026-07-29 -- see the MMC block
#     below. DM_MMC cannot be negated from a defconfig anyway: non-prompted bool,
#     selected by MMC, and MMC is `default ARM`. Turning MMC fully off was worth
#     -12,296 B of u-boot.bin, measured, if it ever needs to go again.)
#   USB_DWC2 (host) — dwc2.c skips a node only for dr_mode == "peripheral", and
#     ours says "otg", so the host driver would bind usb@10180000 and reset the
#     very core the ACM gadget needs (docs/re/USBPLUG-RE.md).
#   ROCKCHIP_GPIO — no DM GPIO consumer exists yet; the LED probe writes GPIO2
#     directly and the sdmmc node has no cd-gpios.
#   SARADC_ROCKCHIP — not inert if enabled: setup_boot_mode() ->
#     rockchip_dnl_key_pressed() (mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c:40) walks UCLASS_ADC
#     and probes the SARADC inside board_late_init, in the window where the boot
#     currently dies. Page-turn ladder keys are a kernel concern.
#   SYS_I2C_ROCKCHIP / DM_PMIC / PMIC_ACT8865 / REGULATOR_ACT8865 — board_init is
#     empty and no power_init_board is defined, so nothing drives a rail. The
#     sdmmc node DOES declare vmmc-supply = <&act_ldo3> and vqmmc-supply =
#     <&vcc_io> (rk3026-onyx-c67ml-magellan.dts:425), but with DM_REGULATOR off
#     those phandles are inert and the controller probes without asking for a
#     regulator. VCC_SD (LDO3) is left as the vendor path left it. Restore this
#     group when the panel or charger needs a rail -- or if the card turns out to
#     need VCC_SD cycled, which is the working theory for why a pin reset skips
#     the SD boot path (docs/HOW-TO.md §5a2).
#   NET_LEGACY / NETDEVICES — no Ethernet exists on this board at all.
#   SYS_ARCH_TIMER — Cortex-A9, no architected timer to enable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

CONFIG_ARM=y
CONFIG_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT=y
# SPL: run cpu_init_cp15, skip only lowlevel_init.
#
# SPL_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT=y skipped BOTH (start.S:118), so the SPL ran with the
# I-cache off and ACTLR.SMP clear, executing from SRAM -- which is why
# sdram_init() and the spin delays are glacial. SPL_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT_ONLY
# keeps lowlevel_init() unreached (we have none to provide) while restoring the
# CP15 init: its own help says "The normal CP15 init (such as enabling the
# instruction cache) is still performed."
#
# Deliberately NOT a cache free-for-all: cpu_init_cp15 CLEARS SCTLR bits 2:0,
# so the MMU and D-cache stay off. It sets only I-cache (bit 12), BTB (bit 11),
# Align (bit 1) and ACTLR bit 6 (SMP/coherency). D-cache in a back-to-BROM SPL
# that hands DRAM back to the mask ROM is a separate, riskier experiment.
# CONFIG_SPL_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT is not set
CONFIG_SPL_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT_ONLY=y
# CONFIG_SPL_USE_ARCH_MEMCPY is not set
# CONFIG_SPL_USE_ARCH_MEMSET is not set
CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP=y
CONFIG_TEXT_BASE=0x60000000
# LTO: TRIED 2026-08-01, DOES NOT BOOT. Saved 664 B of SPL (5640 -> 4976) and
# 13600 B of u-boot-dtb.bin, verify-idbloader passed, and the ARM->Thumb entry
# interworking is intact (blx to the odd-addressed board_init_f), so the classic
# wrong-mode-branch failure is not it. Cause unknown; we build Thumb in both
# phases (SYS_THUMB_BUILD and SPL_SYS_THUMB_BUILD).
# CONFIG_LTO is not set
CONFIG_SPL_LIBGENERIC_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_NR_DRAM_BANKS=1
CONFIG_HAS_CUSTOM_SYS_INIT_SP_ADDR=y
CONFIG_CUSTOM_SYS_INIT_SP_ADDR=0x60100000
CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="rk3026-onyx-c67ml-magellan"
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RK3026=y
CONFIG_SPL_ROCKCHIP_BACK_TO_BROM=y
CONFIG_SPL_STACK_R_ADDR=0x80000
CONFIG_SPL_STACK=0x10081fff
# Payload byte 0 lands at 0x10080800, and mkimage OVERWRITES bytes 0..3 with
# the "RK30" tag, so the first linked word is sacrificial — boot0.h reserves it
# ("b 1f"). The BROM then branches to a fixed 0x10080804. Linking at 0x...804
# instead skews every absolute word by 4 and fails silently. (BROM disassembly.)
CONFIG_SPL_TEXT_BASE=0x10080800
CONFIG_SPL_STACK_R=y
CONFIG_SYS_LOAD_ADDR=0x60800800
CONFIG_PRE_CON_BUF_ADDR=0x60f00000
CONFIG_PRE_CON_BUF_SZ=8192
CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_BASE=0x20068000
# 24 MHz, and it is not a guess: CLKSEL_CON15 bits[9:8] = 2 selects xin24m
# directly, and the vendor console runs with both uart2 dividers gated
# (docs/HARDWARE-CONSTANTS.md). The IP is a DW_apb_uart v3.08a.
CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_CLOCK=24000000
CONFIG_DEBUG_UART=y
# UEFI is an upstream default for armv7 (lib/efi_loader/Kconfig: "default y if
# ... SYS_CPU = armv7"), not something this board asked for. We boot a zImage via
# extlinux/distroboot, never an EFI binary. It also pulls in LMB, DM_EVENT,
# EVENT_DYNAMIC, LIB_UUID and CHARSET, and adds efi_init_early +
# efi_memory_init to board_init_r.
# CONFIG_EFI_LOADER is not set
CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE="rk3026-onyx-c67ml-magellan.dtb"
# PRE_CONSOLE_BUFFER matters as much as the ACM gadget itself: USB cannot
# enumerate until late in board_init_r, so without it every message from before
# that point is lost -- which is exactly the part worth reading.
CONFIG_PRE_CONSOLE_BUFFER=y
CONFIG_CONSOLE_MUX=y
# CONFIG_DISPLAY_CPUINFO is not set
# CONFIG_DISPLAY_BOARDINFO is not set
# Staged LED progress signal (no serial console yet), emitted from
# board_early_init_f / dram_init / misc_init_r, plus an EVT_LAST_STAGE_INIT spy
# (board_late_init is taken by mach-rockchip/board.c).
CONFIG_BOARD_EARLY_INIT_F=y
CONFIG_LAST_STAGE_INIT=y
# Non-blocking LED heartbeat instead of blocking dwells; see boox-c67ml.c.
CONFIG_CYCLIC=y
# Cyclic in the SPL too. Its help names LED blinking as the example use, and it
# needs exactly what now exists: get_timer_us() from the framework timebase, and
# something calling schedule() -- udelay() does (lib/time.c:212), and the DDR
# poll loops in sdram_rk3026.c were given schedule() so a hang inside one keeps
# the LED moving instead of freezing it.
# scripts/Makefile.xpl:121 only descends into common/ for the SPL under
# LIBCOMMON_SUPPORT, and cyclic.o lives there. console.o is separately gated on
# SPL_SERIAL (common/Makefile:76), which stays off, so this does not drag the
# printf/serial chain back in.
CONFIG_SPL_LIBCOMMON_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_SPL_CYCLIC=y
CONFIG_MISC_INIT_R=y
# Back-to-BROM SPL: the mask ROM (not the SPL) loads U-Boot proper, so the SPL
# only inits UART+timer, trains DRAM, and returns. It never calls spl_init().
#
# The SPL is therefore DM-INERT, not DM-free -- CONFIG_SPL_DM is =y regardless of
# what any defconfig line says. MEASURED 2026-07-29, in case anyone reasons about
# this again instead of building it:
#
#   baseline SPL                                              3872 B
#   + SPL_TIMER + SPL_SYS_MALLOC_SIMPLE                       4240 B  (links)
#   + SPL_FRAMEWORK + SPL_SYS_MALLOC_F + SPL_LIBCOMMON_SUPPORT
#     + SPL_OF_CONTROL + SPL_TIMER + SPL_DM_SERIAL           13532 B
#
# against a 6144 B SRAM window.
#
# STALE AS AN ARGUMENT -- corrected 2026-08-07. Read this before quoting 13532.
# That number is FULL SPL_OF_CONTROL with a live fdt, which is not the shape
# upstream recommends for a constrained SPL, and SPL_OF_PLATDATA was measured on
# 2026-08-01 (docs/UPSTREAM-ALIGNMENT.md section 4):
#
#   SPL_OF_CONTROL + SPL_OF_PLATDATA + SPL_OF_REAL            4288 B  FITS
#     (1856 B headroom; DM + dtoc platform data costs 416 B)
#
# So "the SPL is too small for DM" is RETIRED. It is also not hypothetical: this
# config already carries SPL_DM plus SPL_DM_I2C/MMC/SERIAL/SPI/SPI_FLASH/USB and
# SPL_DM_INLINE_OFNODE in a ~3.6 KB binary. What is true is only that
# SPL_OF_PLATDATA is not switched ON here yet -- it depends on SPL_OF_CONTROL
# (dts/Kconfig:450), which is off below. Turning it on is the next step, not
# another measurement.
#
# NOTE the 6144 B bound is not enforced by the build: SPL_MAX_SIZE and
# SPL_SIZE_LIMIT are both 0x0, so an overflow links cleanly and fails on
# hardware.
#
# The link prerequisites, if you retry full OF_CONTROL:
# SPL_SYS_MALLOC_F depends on SPL_FRAMEWORK; malloc_simple.o (which has calloc)
# lives in common/ and needs SPL_LIBCOMMON_SUPPORT; the legacy serial core needs
# default_serial_console unless SPL_DM_SERIAL is on.
# CONFIG_SPL_FRAMEWORK is not set
CONFIG_SPL_NO_BSS_LIMIT=y
CONFIG_SPL_HAVE_INIT_STACK=y
# CONFIG_SPL_DOS_PARTITION is not set
# CONFIG_SPL_EFI_PARTITION is not set
# No Ethernet exists on this board -- not a port, not a PHY, not a USB NIC in the
# boot path -- yet NET is an upstream default, and initr_net runs inside
# board_init_r (board_r.c:823), in the window where the boot currently dies.
# CONFIG_NET is not set
CONFIG_SYSCON=y
# See the ADC note in the header block: enabling this probes the SARADC from
# board_late_init, inside the failing window.
# CONFIG_ADC is not set
CONFIG_CLK=y
# I2C is ON as of 2026-07-30, which is the "restore this group when the panel or
# charger needs a rail" case the header block anticipated: the EPD rails are
# unreachable without it (docs/BLOCKERS.md item 4).
#
# DM_PMIC / DM_REGULATOR stay OFF deliberately, so this is one variable: with
# DM_REGULATOR off the sdmmc node's vmmc-supply/vqmmc-supply phandles remain
# inert and MMC behaviour cannot shift underneath the i2c test. The act8931,
# tps65185 and cyttsp nodes have no matching driver either, so only the two i2c
# CONTROLLERS probe.
CONFIG_DM_I2C=y
CONFIG_SYS_I2C_ROCKCHIP=y
CONFIG_PINCTRL=y
# CONFIG_DM_REGULATOR is not set
# DM serial provides default_serial_console; the legacy core (drivers/serial/
# serial.c) does not, and common/stdio.o -- unconditional in common/, which
# LIBCOMMON pulls in for cyclic.o -- references it. So this is the cost of
# SPL_CYCLIC, not a console: UART2 is still unsoldered.
CONFIG_SPL_DM_SERIAL=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_SHIFT=2
CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_ANNOUNCE=y
CONFIG_SYS_NS16550_MEM32=y
CONFIG_SYSRESET=y
# CONFIG_SPL_SYSRESET is not set
CONFIG_TIMER=y
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_TIMER=y
# A9 MPCore global timer: 64-bit, and its driver reads the halves with a
# high/low/high retry, unlike the rockchip timer which needed that fixed.
# Requires /chosen/tick-timer, supplied in the -u-boot.dtsi.
CONFIG_ARM_GLOBAL_TIMER=y
# USB CDC-ACM console. The OTG controller (usb@10180000, dwc2) is the only
# bidirectional channel this board has without soldering to the UART leads.
#
# CONFIG_USB itself must stay: the whole gadget menu, ACM console included, is
# inside `if USB` (drivers/usb/Kconfig:35..188). Turning it off silently took the
# console with it. DM_USB likewise -- USB_GADGET selects it.
CONFIG_USB=y
CONFIG_USB_GADGET=y
CONFIG_USB_GADGET_MANUFACTURER="ONYX"
CONFIG_USB_GADGET_PRODUCT_NUM=0x0010
CONFIG_USB_GADGET_DWC2_OTG=y
CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ACM=y
# Fastboot is not a board choice -- arch/arm/Kconfig:2114 has
# `imply USB_FUNCTION_FASTBOOT` under ARCH_ROCKCHIP, which then
# `select FASTBOOT`, which `imply ANDROID_BOOT_IMAGE` and `imply CMD_FASTBOOT`.
# An imply loses to an explicit negation, so one line removes the chain.
#
# We do not use it: flashing goes over rockusb/rkflashtool in the vendor loader,
# and the interactive channel is the ACM console. It is also the symbol whose
# defaults list had no ROCKCHIP_RK3026 entry and caused the infinite
# FASTBOOT_BUF_ADDR reprompt documented in docs/HOW-TO.md §0.
#
# Measured: 318,080 -> 302,816 B of u-boot.bin (-15,264).
#
# ⚠️ USB_GADGET_DOWNLOAD MUST BE SET EXPLICITLY, AND THAT IS WHY THE LINE BELOW
# EXISTS. Dropping fastboot alone silently kills the console:
#
#   - USB_FUNCTION_ACM is declared INSIDE `if USB_GADGET_DOWNLOAD`
#     (drivers/usb/gadget/Kconfig:193-232), so it is not even selectable
#     without it -- it disappears from .config entirely rather than turning off.
#   - USB_GADGET_DOWNLOAD is a prompted bool with NO default, and the only
#     `select USB_GADGET_DOWNLOAD` in the whole tree is drivers/fastboot/Kconfig:25.
#   - f_acm.c:646 calls g_dnl_register("usb_serial_acm").
#
# So the ACM console had been standing on fastboot by accident. Caught in the
# build, not on hardware: the first attempt produced a card whose u-boot.bin was
# 37,496 B smaller because it had lost the console stack, which would have
# presented as the 2026-07-30 "board alive, console dead" regression.
CONFIG_USB_GADGET_DOWNLOAD=y
# CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_FASTBOOT is not set
# The A9 global timer counts UP; the old SPL counter counted down.
# CONFIG_SYS_TIMER_COUNTS_DOWN is not set
CONFIG_SPL_TINY_MEMSET=y
# MMC, re-enabled 2026-07-29. It was off because initr_mmc (board_r.c:748) runs
# BEFORE console_init_r (:780) and the dwmmc probe hung in the CRU clock lookup,
# which made the USB ACM console unreachable. That hang was the timer wedge --
# BUS_PCLK/BUS_HCLK misprogrammed off an unlocked PLL -- and get_timer() is now
# confirmed working on hardware (docs/BLOCKERS.md). MMC is what lets U-Boot read
# a zImage off the FAT partition, so this is the step from "we have a prompt" to
# "we can boot a kernel". Verify at the prompt with `mmc info` and `fatls mmc 0:1`.
# CMD_FAT needs no line: it is implied once FS_FAT comes in, and savedefconfig
# drops it. fatls/fatload are present -- verified in the built .config.
CONFIG_MMC_DW=y
CONFIG_MMC_DW_ROCKCHIP=y
CONFIG_CMD_MMC=y
# Bring-up diagnostics reachable from the ACM console. `mmc dev` fails silently
# (cmd/mmc.c returns CMD_RET_FAILURE with no print), so the state it depends on
# has to be readable some other way.
#
# ⚠️ Two corrections to the reasoning that first put these here (2026-07-31):
#
#  - CMD_CLK does NOT "show whether sclk_sdmmc resolved". `clk dump` walks CLK
#    uclass UDEVICES, and UCLASS_DRIVER(clk) has no per_device_auto, so it cannot
#    see CRU-derived rates at all -- it prints only `xin24m`, echoing a DT
#    property back. Read the CRU directly instead: `md.l 0x20000000 0x15` and
#    `md.l 0x200000d0 0xa`. Kept because it is nearly free, not because it works
#    as advertised.
#  - "this port has no Rockchip pinctrl driver" is stale: pinctrl-rk3026.c landed
#    2026-07-30 (fdb5b10) and is proven, with introspection ops, so
#    `pinmux status <pin>` is the better pad read-out. CMD_GPIO stays, but note
#    no GPIO *driver* is enabled yet, so it lists no banks -- ROCKCHIP_GPIO is
#    queued to fix that.
# Boot timing, so boot-speed work has a NUMBER instead of an impression.
#
# This was off by accident, not by decision -- it has no default and nobody
# enabled it. The SPL cpu_init_cp15 change (4f1d302f) was committed with
# "did the boot feel quicker?" as its only success metric, which is not a
# measurement. `bootstage report` gives per-stage timings; CMD_BOOTSTAGE also
# un/stashes them.
#
# Upstream infrastructure, none of it ours. Costs a timestamp per checkpoint.
CONFIG_BOOTSTAGE=y
CONFIG_BOOTSTAGE_REPORT=y
CONFIG_CMD_BOOTSTAGE=y
CONFIG_CMD_CLK=y
# `icache` / `dcache` -- read-outs, not inferences. Two things need them:
#
#  1. Nothing in this port can currently read SCTLR.I back, so the 2026-07-31
#     SPL cpu_init_cp15 change is committed with its effect UNVERIFIED. `icache`
#     prints the state directly.
#  2. `go` at the prompt executes stale memory: U-Boot proper runs with the
#     D-cache on, so `mw.l` lands in the D-cache and `md.l` reads it back
#     correctly while the instruction fetcher sees the old bytes. That is what
#     made the CNTFRQ probe jump into garbage on 2026-07-31. `dcache flush`
#     (or `dcache off`) before `go` fixes it.
CONFIG_CMD_CACHE=y
CONFIG_CMD_GPIO=y
# `i2c dev N; i2c probe` is the whole point of enabling i2c during bring-up: it
# independently checks the four controller base addresses, the pinctrl groups and
# the PCLK_I2C gates all at once, against slaves whose addresses are known
# device-tier (docs/HARDWARE-CONSTANTS.md §9).
CONFIG_CMD_I2C=y
# Reads the kernel's text log out of DRAM. The booted kernel has no console, so
# it writes its findings (devices_deferred and its reasons, above all) to plain
# DRAM at 0x64001000 and reboots back here -- DRAM survives the SPL's DDR
# retraining, measured 2026-08-01. `md.b` would print that as a hex dump with an
# ASCII gutter, hundreds of lines for a few KB; `strings` prints it as text.
CONFIG_CMD_STRINGS=y
# No autoboot during bring-up: -1 means "never autoboot, wait for input", so the
# prompt is always reachable.
#
# Learned the moment MMC came back, 2026-07-29. BOOTCOMMAND is "bootflow scan",
# and with BOOTDELAY=2 that fired two seconds after the banner and scanned the
# new mmc bootdev -- reading partitions and sitting in MMC retries, which
# presented as an unresponsive console that would not take keystrokes. Before MMC
# there was nothing to scan, so the same config dropped to a prompt immediately
# and hid this. There is no kernel on the card yet, so autoboot has nothing to do
# that is worth losing the prompt over; type `bootflow scan` when it is wanted.
CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=-1
# MMC command tracing: OFF as of 2026-08-03, its job is done.
#
# It was added because U-Boot hides the one thing we needed: `mmc dev 0` returns
# SILENTLY on failure -- __init_mmc_device() (cmd/mmc.c) does
# `if (mmc_init(mmc)) return NULL;` with no print, and do_mmc_dev then returns
# CMD_RET_FAILURE printing nothing either. On 2026-07-29 `mmc list` showed
# mmc@10214000:0, `mmc dev 0` printed NOTHING, and `fatls mmc 0:1` said "Bad
# device specification" -- the controller bound and mmc_init() failed invisibly.
#
# The card initialises now, and the trace costs ~1300 lines per `bootflow scan`,
# which buries everything that matters -- on 2026-08-03 it made a boot log
# unreadable while chasing a dead console. It also produced the one fact worth
# keeping: the 32 GB SanDisk answers ACMD41 with OCR 0xc0ff8000
# (docs/HOW-TO.md §6a), which is why that card boots the conventional LBA-64
# copy rather than needing the OCR-shifted one.
#
# Re-add it if mmc_init() ever fails silently again; nothing else reports that.
# CONFIG_MMC_TRACE is not set

# Read the kernel's ramoops log from the U-Boot prompt.
#
# This is the consumer ramoops needs: if a console exists the kernel's own
# dmesg is enough, so the only case ramoops matters is the one where there is
# no console -- and then the reader has to be the stage that still has one.
# U-Boot already ships the command (cmd/pstore.c), so nothing is hand-written.
#
# `strings` is NOT a substitute and must not be used on this region: do_strings
# tests its end address only AFTER each string completes, so text without a
# trailing double NUL runs past the bound and wedges the console. That happened
# on 2026-08-03. `pstore display console` reads the persistent_ram header and
# prints exactly prb->size bytes, handling the wrapped case properly.
#
# Values MATCH the ramoops node in the board dts -- 1 MiB at 0x64100000,
# console-only. record/ftrace/pmsg are 0 there, so they are 0 here; with no
# dump zones the console ring starts at the base address. If the dts changes,
# these must change with it or `pstore display` reads the wrong offset.
#
# `pstore save mmc 0:1 /` writes it to the FAT boot partition, which beats
# pasting hex out of the console.
CONFIG_CMD_PSTORE=y
CONFIG_CMD_PSTORE_MEM_ADDR=0x64100000
CONFIG_CMD_PSTORE_MEM_SIZE=0x100000
CONFIG_CMD_PSTORE_RECORD_SIZE=0x0
CONFIG_CMD_PSTORE_CONSOLE_SIZE=0x100000
CONFIG_CMD_PSTORE_FTRACE_SIZE=0x0
CONFIG_CMD_PSTORE_PMSG_SIZE=0x0
CONFIG_CMD_PSTORE_ECC_SIZE=0
